+\subsection{Domain-Adapted Baseline Comparison}\label{sec:sota}
+SegFormer-B2 and DeepLabV3-R101 were fine-tuned from public pretrained weights on the 2,522-tile LoveDA training split at $560\times560$ (AdamW, lr $=1.5\times10^{-4}$, 3 epochs) and scored with StrongDINOv2Seg on a 100-tile Rural validation subset against official pixel-level ground truth (classes 1--7; T4, batch 1). This is \emph{equal LoveDA training data under a short fixed 3-epoch schedule}, not identical tuning budgets: StrongDINOv2Seg is the epoch-4 checkpoint selected on validation mIoU, which favours it. Table~\ref{tab:sota} is scored on the 100-tile subset, so its 43.11\% mIoU must not be compared with the 53.80\% mIoU (68.91\% mDice) of Table~\ref{tab:seg} on the full validation split.
